INT. CORAL-FARM SUBMERSIBLE - MAINTENANCE BAY - NIGHT

A cramped steel room lit by blue emergency strips. Pipes sweat. Through a thick porthole, a school of luminous fish drifts past.

ILSA VANTERPOOL (40s, chief technician, grease on her forearms) kneels at an open floor panel, welding a coolant line. A radio hisses at her hip. She works with the patience of someone who has done this a thousand times.

Behind her, the hatch wheel TURNS. Slowly. Ilsa freezes, torch still lit.

The hatch swings open. A figure ducks through, dripping. This is KESTREL (30s, drifter, ragged survival suit, a shock baton at his belt). He closes the hatch behind him and looks at her.

ILSA
You're not on the manifest.

KESTREL
Neither is half this boat.

ILSA
How did you get through the lock?

KESTREL
Same way you'd leave. Carefully.

Ilsa shuts off the torch. Sets it down. Stands, slowly, wiping her hands on her thighs. He watches the movement. She watches his baton.

ILSA
Captain doesn't allow guests.

KESTREL
Captain's asleep.

ILSA
Captain doesn't sleep.

KESTREL
Then he's dead. Take your pick.

She lunges for the radio. He crosses the bay in two steps and grabs her wrist. They struggle, knocking a toolbox off the wall, spanners clattering. She drives an elbow into his ribs. He grunts, twists, slams her against the pipe. Both of them freeze, breathing hard, faces inches apart.

ILSA
Let go.

KESTREL
Only if you stay quiet.

ILSA
I won't.

KESTREL
Then I won't let go.

The pipe behind her starts to HISS. A thin jet of steam. Both of them stare at it. Then at each other. The coolant line she was welding is failing.

ILSA
That's the main feed.

KESTREL
Fix it.

ILSA
Let me go and I will.

He hesitates. The steam thickens. The fish outside scatter. He lets go. She drops to her knees and grabs the torch, and he crouches beside her, holding the pipe steady with his bare gloves, wincing at the heat.

ILSA (CONT'D)
Hold it. Tighter.

KESTREL
It's burning.

ILSA
Then burn.

The torch flares. The weld glows. The hiss dies. They look at each other, soaked, shaking, and neither moves away.
